        "original_id": "ef3f46f6-e81c-54d7-8365-491047df8c29",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Entwistle\n- Organizations: The Who\n- Products: Tommy, Pinball Wizard, Overture, Underture, Sparks\n- Topics: music releases, chart performance, band roles\n\nFacts:\n- The Who released their fourth studio album, the double album Tommy, in May 1969.\n- Pinball Wizard was released as a single in 1969 and reached No. 4 in the UK charts and No. 19 on the U.S. Billboard Hot 100.\n- Overture is one of three instrumental tracks on Tommy, alongside Underture and Sparks, although Overture includes some lyrics toward the end.\n- John Entwistle was best known during a music career spanning more than 40 years as the original bass guitarist for the English rock band The Who.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
